#Algorithm
Step 1: Start.

Step 2: Enter the password to be validated.

Step 3: Initialize the password status as valid.

Step 4: Check whether the password meets the minimum length requirement. If not, display the minimum length error.

Step 5: Check whether the password contains the required character categories, such as uppercase letters, lowercase letters, digits, and special characters. Display an error for each missing category.

Step 6: Check whether the password contains repeated characters beyond the permitted limit. If yes, display the repetition error.

Step 7: Check whether the password contains any prohibited substring. If yes, display the prohibited-substring error.

Step 8: If any condition fails, mark the password as invalid. Otherwise, mark it as valid.

Step 9: Display the password validation result and the reasons for each failed condition.

Step 10: Stop.

